# Files copied into every git worktree (--worktree, isolation: worktree
# subagents, desktop parallel sessions). Only files that match AND are
# gitignored get copied.
#
# Why this file exists: a worktree gets tracked files only. .claude/ and
# .agent-context/ are gitignored, so without this an agent in a worktree
# starts with no Stop hook, no test sensor, and no permissions.deny —
# isolated AND unsupervised, the worst combination.
#
# Do NOT replace this with a WorktreeCreate hook: that replaces git worktree
# creation wholesale and disables .worktreeinclude processing entirely.

.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.agent-context/hooks/**
.agent-context/scripts/**
.agent-context/skills/run_skill.sh
.agent-context/project.md
.agent-context/conventions.md
.agent-context/domain.md
.agent-context/pipeline-contract.md

# Deliberately excluded:
#   status.json, intercom.jsonl, memory/, .heal_state — per-run state; copying
#     it makes two worktrees believe they are the same run.
#   skills/<slug>/ — shared success/fail counters would race.
#   .env, *.db, qdrant_storage/ — no reason for a code-editing worktree to
#     hold another copy of secrets or local data.
#   .venv/ — too large; run_tests.sh falls back to python3.
